     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi,</div><div><br></div><div><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:16.9px;background-color:rgba(252,251,248,0.901961)\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"padding-right:15px;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"text-align:center;min-width:46px\"><span title=\"View upvote and downvote totals\" style=\"margin-top:8px;margin-bottom:8px;font-size:20px;display:block;color:rgb(106,115,124)\"><br></span><a title=\"This question does not show any research effort; it is unclear or not useful\" style=\"margin-right:auto;margin-bottom:10px;margin-left:auto;font-size:1px;color:rgb(189,69,26);overflow:hidden;display:block;width:40px;min-height:40px;background-image:url(&quot;&quot;),none;background-size:initial;background-position:0px -220px;background-repeat:no-repeat\" rel=\"nofollow\">down vote</a><a href=\"http://stats.stackexchange.com/questions/212722/overestimated-mcmc-standard-deviation-sd#\" title=\"Click to mark as favorite question (click again to undo)\" style=\"margin-right:auto;margin-bottom:2px;margin-left:auto;font-size:1px;color:rgb(189,69,26);overflow:hidden;display:block;width:40px;min-height:30px;background-image:url(&quot;&quot;),none;background-size:initial;background-position:0px -120px;background-repeat:no-repeat\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stats.stackexchange.com/questions/212722/overestimated-mcmc-standard-deviation-sd%23&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461480454000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0LeA10iT-FgvHb6gS4ycAk\">favorite</a><div><span style=\"color:rgb(106,115,124)\"></span></div></div></td><td style=\"vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;font-size:15px;width:660px;word-wrap:break-word;line-height:1.3\"><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;clear:both\">I did a simulation study with 100 replications for a complex model with <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(239,240,241)\">rstan</code>, and I found the standard deviation (SD) of posterior samples is larger than the true value. This seems to depend on the number of chains.</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;clear:both\">The idea is that, I simulated 100 data sets from a model. For each data set, I fit it with <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(239,240,241)\">rstan</code>, and I save the point estimate (of <span style=\"color:inherit\"></span><span role=\"presentation\" style=\"display:inline;line-height:normal;word-spacing:normal;word-wrap:normal;white-space:nowrap;float:none;direction:ltr;max-width:none;max-height:none;min-width:0px;min-height:0px\"><u></u><span role=\"math\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:0px;width:0.762em\"><span style=\"font-size:18.45px;display:inline-block;vertical-align:0px;width:0.599em;min-height:0px\"><span style=\"font-size:18.45px;vertical-align:0px\"><span style=\"font-size:18.45px;display:inline;vertical-align:0px\"><span style=\"font-size:18.45px;display:inline;vertical-align:0px;font-family:MathJax_Math-italic\">β<span style=\"font-size:18.45px;display:inline-block;vertical-align:0px;overflow:hidden;min-height:1px;width:0.003em\"></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:18.45px;display:inline-block;vertical-align:0px;width:0px;min-height:2.171em\"></span></span></span><span style=\"border-left-style:solid;display:inline-block;vertical-align:-0.33em;overflow:hidden;width:0px;min-height:1.27em\"></span></span><u></u></span><span style=\"line-height:1.3\">) and standard deviation of the posterior samples in</span><span style=\"line-height:1.3\"> </span><code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(239,240,241)\">est_b</code><span style=\"line-height:1.3\"> </span><span style=\"line-height:1.3\">and</span><span style=\"line-height:1.3\"> </span><code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(239,240,241)\">sd_b</code><span style=\"line-height:1.3\">respectively. So</span><span style=\"line-height:1.3\"> </span><code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(239,240,241)\">est_b</code><span style=\"line-height:1.3\"> </span><span style=\"line-height:1.3\">and</span><span style=\"line-height:1.3\"> </span><code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(239,240,241)\">sd_b</code><span style=\"line-height:1.3\"> </span><span style=\"line-height:1.3\">are both a vector of 100 elements.</span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;clear:both\">If I use the default setting (<code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(239,240,241)\">chains = 4, iter = 2000</code>) in <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(239,240,241)\">rstan</code>, the average calculated SD in a single replication (<code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(239,240,241)\">mean(sd_b))</code> is higher than the true SD (<code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(239,240,241)\">sd(est_b)</code>, SD of 100 point estimates, we treated this as the true value of SD).</p><pre style=\"margin-bottom:1em;padding:5px;font-size:13px;width:auto;max-height:600px;overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;color:rgb(57,51,24);word-wrap:normal;background-color:rgb(239,240,241)\"><code style=\"font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:inherit\"><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\"> mean</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">sd_b</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(125,39,39)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">]</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(125,39,39)\">0.4838592</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\"> sd</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">est_b</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(125,39,39)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">]</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(125,39,39)\">0.4376797</span></code></pre><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;clear:both\">If I use only 1 chain but <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(239,240,241)\">iter = 4*2000</code>, the two metrics seem similar.</p><pre style=\"margin-bottom:1em;padding:5px;font-size:13px;width:auto;max-height:600px;overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;color:rgb(57,51,24);word-wrap:normal;background-color:rgb(239,240,241)\"><code style=\"font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:inherit\"><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\"> mean</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">sd_b</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(125,39,39)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">]</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(125,39,39)\">0.4740169</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\"> sd</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">est_b</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(125,39,39)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">]</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(125,39,39)\">0.4712312</span></code></pre><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;clear:both\">I also tried 8 chains but got similar result as 4 chains. I am wondering if anyone has confronted this kind of problem before, or has an explanation / solution for this, and I am also not sure if this issue is <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(239,240,241)\">Stan</code> specific. I can share the code and data if an reproducible example is needed.</p></div></td></tr></tbody></table><br></div><div>Thanks a lot,</div><div>Randel</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
}
